The XRD data in Fig. 3
                      show that Kaolin0 exhibited mainly one strong peak at 2θ ≈ 20.04°, which corresponds to the β-sheet structure of the protein component in SMF [27]. Kaolin alone had some strong peaks with 2θ = 12.28°–38.32°. The peaks at 2θ ≈ 19.76°, 20.24°, and 21.12° belong to the typical 020, 110, and 111 crystal faces of kaolin from the AGFI calculation, respectively [24]. Kaolin30-comp was prepared by evenly and gently mixing kaolin powder with cured Kaolin0 powder in the dry state at room temperature, so it should show no or negligible intercalation, and the kaolin AGFI value (1.24) was similar to the AGFI value of kaolin alone (1.27). In contrast, Kaolin30, which had the same composition but was hybridized under wet conditions, had a much smaller kaolin AGFI (0.92), indicating that the kaolin within it was more disordered (or with less crystallinity) due to the penetration of EMPA and/or unfolded SMF chains within the interlayers of kaolin via the intercalation process (as illustrated in Fig. 4
                     ).
